      "updated": 1785514349274,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "In C++, a cast is an operator that explicitly converts a value from one data type to another,\nwhich is necessary because C++ is a strongly typed language where implicit conversions are\nlimited",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 7,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "In C++, a cast is an operator that explicitly converts a value from one data type to another, which is necessary because C++ is a strongly typed language where implicit conversions are limited",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.15
    },
